  "disclosure": "Measured on the 27 Oct 2026 draw and shown unranked until that draw is equated to the reference scale. The composed decision checkpoint and selected recipe differ from the author Decision Index system-prompt recipe; reported Decision Index numbers are not transferred here. The read-only plugin was registered with a first-party distribution marker without running author build scripts. Composer/tutorial subtrees were excluded; audio limit zero and skip-mm-profiling prevented optional ASR loading. The local shim and vLLM backend communicated over loopback inside a read-only container with no external network, empty credentials, offline flags, read-only mounts and restricted capabilities. A local memory observer read peak CUDA allocator memory without changing tensors or probabilities; the shim could not proxy its dev-RPC route. Source and tokenizer hashes were verified before protected staging. Upstream wheels were hash-locked; Debian libgomp1 12.2.0-14+deb12u1 and libnuma1 2.0.16-1 were recorded. Source checks and isolation are not a full audit of upstream code/custom kernels, a contamination audit, or a minimum-hardware guarantee. Training data and overlap with evaluation data were not independently inspected. The model card and Granite Switch source declare Apache-2.0; the Hugging Face checkpoint contains no standalone LICENSE file. Exact provider deletion of the VM and OS volume and private staging shreds were verified. No scored retry, response repair, permutation averaging or replacement was used. Replay is record-only: 7 of 50 bit-identical, ONE argmax flip, maximum absolute probability difference 0.031222338329561394; this differs from the separately measured 8B row. Whole states and ordered options were preserved, with no truncation/refusal. Native 818,484 input and 1,500 output tokens include all full-prompt chunks. Five requests above ten seconds count as wrong answers. The measured base remains ibm-granite/granite-4.1-30b; the price uses the explicitly labelled granite-4.2-30b sibling estimate, with no invented cross-family throughput, observed-loop extrapolation or pod-bill substitution.",
